# Godot's import cache and generated metadata.
.godot/
*.import

# ...except this one. Left to itself Godot imports locale/kiosk.csv into a
# binary .translation and drops the raw file from the export. The committed
# .import pins it to "keep", so what ships is the CSV a translator can read and
# a player can copy, which is the whole point of the file.
!locale/kiosk.csv.import

# Same for the painted textures. They are read with Image.load at runtime rather
# than as imported resources — the game picks a file per surface and falls back
# to the generator when there is not one — so what has to ship is the PNG, not a
# .ctex compiled from it. Without these, an exported build loads nothing and
# quietly looks exactly like it did before the pack existed.
!textures/*.import

# icon.png / .ico / .icns are generated by tools/MakeIcon.tscn and *are*
# committed, on purpose. Unlike everything else here they have to exist as files
# before the exporters run — Godot writes the .icns into the .app bundle and
# hands the .ico to rcedit at build time, neither of which can happen at
# runtime. The generator is still the source of truth; regenerate rather than
# edit.

# Build output.
build/
export/

# Screenshot harness output.
.shots/

# Editor and OS noise.
.DS_Store
*.swp

# The texture sheets the pack arrived as. Big, and only ever an input to
# tools/CutTextures.tscn — what the game loads is the cut swatches in textures/,
# which are committed.
art/sheets/
